/// `SlowCloseOnPing`: closes on any data. `handleClose:` records whether it
/// could still send, then takes a second, so a test can tell whether the
/// socket was closed before it ran or only after it returned (BT-4655).
RecordingHandler subclass: SlowCloseOnPing

  handleData: _data :: Object socket: _sock :: Socket state: st :: Object -> HandlerResult =>
    HandlerResult close: st

  handleClose: sock :: Socket state: st :: Object -> Object =>
    self note: {#sendInClose, (sock send: "late") isOk}
    Timer sleep: 1000
    super handleClose: sock state: st
